window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Evil comes from a Demon who disappeared long ago and left behind fragments of itself that twist and poison the world. Every wicked deed you’ve ever known, every time the worst of humanity has come to the surface, it’s because of demonic energy. Without the Custodians it’d be so much worse.</p> <p>From a young age Louis was told who he should be. He’s a Custodian and he’s meant to protect humanity from the spread of infection. He’s supposed to be a hero; but for the last fourteen months he’s been stuck in a tiny little town where nothing happens and no one needs him.</p> <p>When he finally gets a new assignment in a new town his life is still a little different to how he pictured it. This doesn’t come naturally to him and he thought it would. Most of his new team hate him, and in the case of the know-it-all Danny it’s mutual. Louis just wants to do Good, but it’s not that simple. He’s going to have to learn the Tragedy of Hazel Hardcastle, get to grips with his own power, confront confusing feelings for brown-eyed boys, and eventually, survive the end of the f**king world.</p>"; 
